Having an ante-natal visit is closely linked to the level of education of the mother. Among women with no
formal education, 60.9 percent received ante-natal care. The higher a women’s educational attainment, the
higher the percentage of women who received ante-natal care. The biggest gap is between women with no
schooling at all (60.9 percent) and women with primary education (83.2 percent). Only small differences

