Ante-natal care gives skilled providers an opportunity to communicate with women about safe motherhood,
maternal and child health and the benefits of family planning. The ALCS 2016-17 allows to evaluate if
women who obtained ante-natal care had higher contraceptive use. This is indeed the case. Contraceptive
use of any method among women who had received ante-natal care was 54.4 percent, against 36.1 percent

