the distribution to those in need. Figure 9.25 shows the percentage of children 0 to 59 months old who
received Vitamin A tablets or capsules, by province. Large differences exist between the provinces in terms
of distribution of Vitamin A, ranging from almost full coverage to virtually no distribution at all. In three
provinces, mothers report ed that almost none of their children get the Vitamin A supplement: Takhar,
Badghis and Baghlan, while in two other provinces less than 20 percent of children were given the
supplement (Nimroz and Ghazni). While slightly more than half of all young children living in Afghanistan
received Vitamin A supplement, in 16 provinces less than half of children did so.

